  /** Internal bridge density — (%) — Controls the density (spacing) of internal bridge lines. Internal bridges act as intermediate support between sparse infill and top solid infill and can strongly affect top surface quality. - Higher than 100% density (Recommended Max 125%): - Pros: Improves internal bridge strength and support under top layers, reducing sagging and improving top-surface finish. - Cons: Increases material use and print time; excessive density may cause overextrusion and internal stresses. - Lower than 100% density (Min 10%): - Pros: Can reduce pillowing and improve cooling (more airflow through the bridge), and may speed up printing. - Cons: May reduce internal support, increasing the risk of sagging and top surface defects. This option works particularly well when combined with the second internal bridge over infill option to improve bridging further before solid infill is extruded. */
